  "caveats": [
    "Measurements cover one macOS 27 arm64 Apple M5 Max host; results are not a cross-platform claim.",
    "S, M, L, XL-single, and PATH-HEAVY are generated fixtures. The generated benchmark matrix REAL row remains unmeasured; separate public-project captures and comparisons are recorded in docs/validation/real-projects.md.",
    "All displayed lcovmerge measurements use a Dataset M-trained Apple Clang profile-guided host build. Release binaries remain portable target builds; this is not a cross-platform speed claim.",
    "lcovmerge timing uses one hyperfine warmup and five measured runs for S, M, L, XL-single, and PATH-HEAVY; XXL uses one warmup and three measured runs. Cache warmups were used, but no explicit cache flush was applied.",
    "lcov 2.6 ran once on the XXL input on 2026-10-12 and completed in 827.629 s; the 2026-10-11 run recorded 1080.632 s on the same host with machine load uncontrolled. Its S, M, L, XL-single, and PATH-HEAVY values are earlier recorded measurements that were not rerun; the PATH-HEAVY run exited with status 1 after 98.805 s, so no valid speedup or current-run peak resident memory is reported for that failure.",
    "lcov-result-merger 6.0.0 did not finish its XXL warmup before the 60-minute cutoff in the 2026-10-11 run and was not rerun for 1.1.0. It was stopped with SIGTERM after 3615.813 s wall time; no measured run completed. Periodic RSS samples peaked at 2.34 GiB, but the full-run peak is unavailable. Other lcov-result-merger rows are earlier measurements made with Node v24.14.0.",
    "Dataset M sorted regular shards use the direct single-threaded path; --jobs timings show run variation, not the effect of adding workers.",
    "grcov 0.10.8 is identified as the current release but was not included in the measured benchmark runs.",
    "The external Bazel issue is context only and was not measured with these commands."
  ],
